It was ten in the morning.
The train slowly moved forward from the station.
I looked at the people around me from my own seat.
There were many passengers in the compartment.
A man sitting opposite me suddenly opened his own bag.
He was very nervous.
He quickly checked both his own pockets.
He was searching for his own ticket.
After a few minutes, he found his own ticket in his shirt pocket.
Seeing the ticket, he calmed down.
On the other side, a small family was sitting.
A little girl and her older brother were sitting together.
There was a snack packet in the boy's hand.
The girl did not have any snack of her own.
She was repeatedly trying to snatch her brother's snack.
She did not want her own food, but his food.
The brother quickly hid his own packet.
I smiled looking at both the children.
Then I brought my own attention back to my window.
